Then add a rule to agents.md to only perform database push and never migrations.

389
00:37:31,534 --> 00:37:34,400
And also remove the migration script from package.json.

390
00:37:34,640 --> 00:37:39,844
You should now have a new entry inside of your agents.md that looks something like this.

391
00:37:40,142 --> 00:37:44,164
It's basically an instruction for agents to avoid using migrations.

392
00:37:44,494 --> 00:37:47,920
Now, migrations are not bad. In fact, they are preferred.

393
00:37:48,014 --> 00:37:53,840
But when it comes to developing a project, they can be quite annoying, especially if conflicts arise.

394
00:37:54,000 --> 00:37:56,676
And it's just going to spend your time and tokens.

395
00:37:56,880 --> 00:38:01,040
The rest of the files are pretty much unchanged except the package.json.

396
00:38:01,280 --> 00:38:09,360
I explicitly told the agent to remove the migration script because I don't want any new agent to accidentally look at that script and think, oh,

397
00:38:09,520 --> 00:38:10,800
I should probably use this.

398
00:38:10,990 --> 00:38:18,640
Now, besides instructing our agent to not do migrations, I would also instruct it to never do backwards compatibility.

399
00:38:18,990 --> 00:38:29,156
So tell your agent to update agent's MD with the fact that this is a development project, meaning there is no backwards compatibility and the data is worthless.

400
00:38:29,454 --> 00:38:30,692
Prefer data loss.

401
00:38:30,894 --> 00:38:37,280
Never backfill, migrate, or preserve existing rows, and never spend effort on keeping old data working.

402
00:38:37,486 --> 00:38:40,132
Every schema change means a clean slate.

403
00:38:40,608 --> 00:38:50,128
I would highly suggest running this prompt and updating Agents, MD according to this rule, because agents are notorious for backwards compatibility

404
00:38:50,288 --> 00:39:01,168
that is unnecessary, because they treat every project as a production project. and they think that every change you do has to be backfilled and backwards compatible.

405
00:39:01,408 --> 00:39:09,408
And that makes very weird and confusing code, which is often associated with AI slop.

406
00:39:09,568 --> 00:39:12,768
Do be careful when you eventually reach production.

407
00:39:12,928 --> 00:39:21,796
At that point, you should most likely remove those rules from your agents.md so they don't drop your production database.

