509
00:49:30,208 --> 00:49:39,236
We don't have to change any environment variables because this was mostly just bot creation. We can now create new bots, but we still can't communicate with them.

510
00:49:39,408 --> 00:49:45,248
In order to achieve that, we need to create an equivalent chat record for every bot that we create.

511
00:49:45,422 --> 00:49:53,808
We can then list those chat records in an application sidebar. And once the user clicks on a chat, they will get redirected to the conversation ID.

512
00:49:53,968 --> 00:50:01,808
This way, bots can exist independently from chats, and chats can also become group chats by adding many bots inside.

513
00:50:01,934 --> 00:50:11,888
Let's tell our agent to add a new chats table, as well as a chat members join table, and the relations for all the tables that we're going to have in our schema.

514
00:50:12,302 --> 00:50:19,108
Chats table will have an ID, user ID, a kind, which is an enum, which can either be direct or group.

515
00:50:19,472 --> 00:50:25,792
Name, which is optional, and it's going to be null for direct chats, in which we're going to use the bot's name directly.

516
00:50:25,872 --> 00:50:28,992
But for group chats, we will be able to give the group a name.

517
00:50:29,232 --> 00:50:33,792
Last message preview to display what's the last message sent in that chat.

518
00:50:33,952 --> 00:50:43,312
Last message at, which is a required, and defaults to now, so we know whether a new message has been sent, and a created add property, which defaults to now.

519
00:50:43,472 --> 00:50:52,992
Then we're going to have the chat members join table. Each chat member should have a chat ID that it belongs to, which should reference the chat table and it should cascade on delete.

520
00:50:53,232 --> 00:50:58,832
Bot ID, which should be indexed, references the bot table and also cascades on delete.

521
00:50:59,072 --> 00:51:04,992
Joined at, and the primary key, which is a composite key of chat ID and bot ID together.

522
00:51:05,152 --> 00:51:06,884
And finally, we define the relations.

523
00:51:07,072 --> 00:51:13,860
A bot has many memberships, a chat has many members, and a chat member has one chat and one bot.

524
00:51:14,032 --> 00:51:23,428
You should now have a new chats table, which has an ID, user ID, kind, which corresponds to a Postgres enum that can either be direct or group,

525
00:51:23,632 --> 00:51:29,472
an optional name, last message preview, last message add created at, and an index for the user ID.

526
00:51:29,552 --> 00:51:36,592
You should also have a chat members table, which has a composite primary key for chat ID and bot ID.

527
00:51:36,686 --> 00:51:40,912
And you should have bots relations, chat relations, and chat member relations.

528
00:51:41,166 --> 00:51:45,392
Now tell your agent to perform a database push, stage, and commit.

529
00:51:45,552 --> 00:51:51,072
Inside of your neon console, besides the bots table, you should have chat members and chats table.

530
00:51:51,152 --> 00:51:59,712
The only problem we have now is that when we create a new bot, it doesn't automatically create a new conversation or chat record.

531
00:51:59,886 --> 00:52:05,892
So I just pushed a new bot and you can see that my chats are still empty, but I have a new bot.

532
00:52:06,190 --> 00:52:14,308
So now we need to modify our bot action to also create a new chat record and a chat member insert.

533
00:52:14,512 --> 00:52:27,748
We can simply tell our agent to modify actions bot to batch create a new bot, new direct chat, and a chat member. Your agent should either use database transaction or database batch for this.

534
00:52:28,014 --> 00:52:35,044
Both work as long as you can see some kind of encapsulation between creating a bot and a chat and inserting the chat members.

535
00:52:35,312 --> 00:52:39,620
This way, a bot cannot exist without its equivalent chat.

536
00:52:39,886 --> 00:52:43,792
And a chat cannot exist without its equivalent chat member insert.

537
00:52:43,952 --> 00:52:47,072
That's why we are doing this within a batch or a transaction.

538
00:52:47,214 --> 00:52:48,868
So we don't have any orphaned bots.

539
00:52:49,152 --> 00:52:57,668
I would now recommend going inside of your neon console and deleting all of your bot records so you can try and test whether this works on a clean slate.

540
00:52:57,838 --> 00:53:01,028
So once again, try and create a new bot.

541
00:53:01,392 --> 00:53:06,912
And this time it should also create an equivalent chat and chat members record.

542
00:53:07,072 --> 00:53:07,552
There we go.

543
00:53:07,712 --> 00:53:09,312
All three records have been added.

