01:27:00,750 --> 01:27:04,580
Go inside of your production instance and open any conversation.

904
01:27:04,736 --> 01:27:09,376
And then shut down your local trigger server that's running.

905
01:27:09,536 --> 01:27:14,016
So make sure nothing is running and try and communicate with your agent.

906
01:27:14,176 --> 01:27:15,172
Let's see what happens.

907
01:27:15,536 --> 01:27:26,816
The agent is infinitely stuck in submitting mode. That is because we're mixing a Next.js production instance who is trying to connect to our local trigger server.

908
01:27:26,976 --> 01:27:35,748
So we have to create a production trigger instance and then create the new trigger secret key and add that to railway deployment.

909
01:27:36,096 --> 01:27:42,656
And then the trigger server will be running independently somewhere else and not on our machine.

910
01:27:42,830 --> 01:27:47,616
So go back inside of your trigger dashboard and switch from development to production.

